message: "If you use or build on ECONOVA-S™, please cite this repository."
title: "ECONOVA-S: A Dual-Core Scientific Economic Intelligence Platform for Governed AI Scientific Discovery in Economics and Finance"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Homayoun"
    given-names: "Saeid"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2536-0446"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Saehon/Saeid-Homayoun"
abstract: >-
  ECONOVA-S is a dual-core scientific economic intelligence platform built around Canonical Architecture V2.5. It separates a Stable Economic Knowledge Core from a Replaceable Technology Core and uses a supporting AI-to-AI Scientific Intelligence Fabric for governed hypothesis generation, ERA-style empirical conversion, AlphaEvolve-inspired specification search, evidence-grounded RAG, econometric testing, independent red-team review, replication, falsification, welfare interpretation, Evidence Passport construction, and explicit human approval. Software release v0.2.0 adds real-data ingestion paths, evidence metadata retrieval, six-table empirical reporting, temporal out-of-sample checks, Stata export, and a non-bypassable discovery gate. POC and prototype outputs are research-workbench evidence only; discovery_claim_allowed remains false until real-data provenance, construct validation, credible identification, replication or appropriate out-of-sample evidence, economic significance, welfare validation, and human scientific judgment are satisfied.
keywords:
